This directory holds two kinds of file, and they sit under one licence for one
reason: the corpus they draw on requires it.

  data/overrides.toml   corrections to the corpus, keyed on a source folder
  data/decisions.tsv    the shipped filename-to-decision table

Licence: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0)
         https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

Attribution: Grand Comics Database™ (https://www.comics.org)

The Grand Comics Database content is licensed CC BY-SA 4.0, and share-alike
propagates into anything derived from it. `data/overrides.toml` exists only to
correct the corpus, so it is derived by construction.

`data/decisions.tsv` is a mixture, and this file does not try to separate it.
Every row was confirmed by a human — nothing is stored without a keystroke
(D49, D51) — but the proposal a human confirmed is often the corpus's, and on
the reviewed Humble table 239 of 2,223 rows had a field decided by a corpus
lookup (the series casing of D62, the colon confirmations of the 2026-10-25
research). Splitting the table by provenance per field would be a worse
document than covering all of it, and share-alike is the safe direction: it
grants more than a bare factual table would need, never less.

What this licence does not do is grant a right nobody holds. A licence governs
what others may do with work that is ours to give; it says nothing about
whether a given body of data was ours to publish. For anything derived from a
marketplace's own records — order histories, catalogue exports — that question
is answered by that marketplace's terms, not here.

Share-alike applies to this directory only. The program's source code is
GPL-3.0-or-later (see ../LICENSE), which D3/D9 of the design document records
as a deliberate split.
